Z||000008||wkayl||04-28-2000||09:00 AM||||I don't have the 1st car I had (1953 Ford Mainline 4 door), but who would want it.  When I was a Sr. in HS I bought a 1961 Studebaker.  I drove the wheels off it untill it just wouldn't go any more.  1 year after I got out of school (Class of '73)I had the chance to get another one just like it except this one had an automatic. It was the same model, color and everything else.  I still have it.  My son came home from the hospital in it, was the 1st car he ever drove, and the 1st car he drove when he turned 16 and was legal to drive.  It even passed Colorado emmisions.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Studebaker.jpg">  <P>I have replaced the engine and transmission, but all else is original, even the paint.<p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Old Lar||04-28-2000||11:07 AM||||It helps to be a millionare.  As everyone says these are 13-16 year old cars.  and if you want to keep them going, you have to "rebuild" them continually if you want to drive them.  I got my first Fiero new when I was 40, so I had a nest egg and with no wife as a cash drain, I could indulge.  You make choices in this world.  The Fiero was more reliable than the wife.  I've had the Fiero longer than I had the wife, and with less problems.||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||04-28-2000||01:34 PM||||don't have to be a millionare.. just disciplined enough not so spend your money on other things... I'm a College student too! Who are you gunna work with in the CNC industery. I have friends in that same field. Working for Jones & Shippman,  Brown&Sharpe, Flint machine tool and Makita. Ive found in th  3 years at Ga. Tech that  Beer is essential... toilet paper.. and your car... everything else is elective.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||WKDFIRO||04-28-2000||03:01 PM||||Just like the hot rodders I would say that most of us are tinkerers. Seeing your 87 made me sigh. My first car was an 87 coupe the exact color as yours. I was so excited when I got it. Up until it was destroyed I was tinkering with it. Being a millionare sure helps but it is not essential. Fieros have already proven to be good past the 300 k and still going strong. Very few people really appreciate the Fiero so when I still have my Fiero when Im old and grey I doubt the motorheads will really care. Right up to the point when I fire it up. <P>"Oh yeah its just a V6, Ive just been tinkering with it for a few years..."<P>When I look in the mirror and past the tire smoke, I just treasure the look on their faces. Just a Fiero. Right. ||||reg||6
Z||000012||lennyb4||04-28-2000||03:21 PM||||HEY!!! I found my cars twin.. My 87 is exectly the same. But to the point im far from rich, its like WLDFIRO said i just tinker with it when ever i get spare money. My interior is horid but sooner or later i will get it all done.But its still a hell of alot of fun to drive...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
